        "assemblyNotes": "Touch-the-lands CBTO in the MPR: 2.931 in (most common of 2.931, 2.939, 2.931). Seat to CBTO 2.911 in for 0.020 in jump. ELD-X is not jump sensitive; 0.020 in off is the usual starting point. Measure with the same .30 cal comparator insert the sheet was measured with; re-check touch every few hundred rounds as the throat wears.",
        "notes": "Hornady #3077, .308 in, 212 gr ELD-X. Published G7 .336 / G1 .673. Starting profile: powder, charge, primer, brass and velocity are blank until the workup. Bullet length 1.600 in (estimate; Hornady does not publish it) only feeds the spin-drift term.",
